values ('c4d5e6f7-8a9b-4c11-8e11-1f2a3b4c5d11', 'music-history-ii-classical-romantic', 'Music History II (Classical-Romantic)', 'Music History II surveys Western art music from the galant and Classical style through late Romanticism. Students study Haydn, Mozart, Beethoven, Schubert, Schumann, Verdi, Wagner, Brahms, Tchaikovsky, Mahler, Strauss, and other central figures while also asking how institutions, technology, markets, gender, nation, empire, criticism, and performance practice shaped the repertory. The course balances listening, score study, primary sources, historical writing, and performance-aware analysis. Students learn not only to identify styles and works, but to explain why a musical event mattered in its own social world and how later canons made it matter differently.');

